    "updated_at": "2026-11-12T09:36:13Z",
    "body": "Merged `issue/533-wire-iso-post` (#1139) into this branch to resolve the combined conflicts (`posting_wire.rs` add/add, `posting.rs`, `wire_contour.rs`: keep both sides) - merge `8cd0aff6`, no rebase, no force-push.\n\n- `posting_wire.rs`: one module holding #533's `stream` (op_streams' wire section) and #534's `wire_clause` (verification_report); `posting.rs` mounts it once as `wire` and re-exports `wire_clause`, `WireClause`, `WIRE_VERDICT`.\n- `wire_contour.rs`: asserts the machine note now says the wire laws judge at the post AND the wire cut streams with `EdmCondition C110`.\n- New `test(app)` `3e852d68`: `wire_post::the_wire_laws_stand_between_the_cut_and_its_nc_text` - a clean punch posts through `wire-iso.cps` to #533's golden (unchanged) with the wire verdict on the not-judged line; a die whose kerf burns the plate above its opening still streams but `post_script` refuses it by name (`Die1: wire gouge: ...`) and writes no NC file.\n\nGate on head `3e852d68`: `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/issue/533-wire-iso-post` green (4 steps, 0 failed, 10.4 min; `wire_post` 5, `wire_contour` 7, `wire_verify` 3 among the app suites); `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean. PR is now stacked on #1139.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
